    <bpmn:process id="W_W3119" name="W3119. Cooperative Livelihood Program &amp; Government Partnership" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New community identified; government livelihood-program cycle (DSWD-SLP, DOLE livelihood, DTI-BMED, TESDA)
Frequency: Annual + event-driven
Volume: ~3–8 active partnerships
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Sustainability Lead, Sustainability Sourcing Mgr, Government Agency Liaison, Coop Representatives, Legal
Source: workflow W3119 — Cooperative Livelihood Program &amp; Government Partnership</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3119_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3119_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3119_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3119_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3119_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3119_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3119_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3119_Start3" name="New community identified; government livelihood-program cycle (DSWD-SLP, DOLE livelihood…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3119_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3119_Task4" name="Sustainability Lead/Agency Liaison engage government livelihood programs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sustainability Lead/Agency Liaison engage government livelihood programs: DSWD-SLP (Sustainable Livelihood Program), DOLE livelihood, DTI-BMED (Bureau of MSME Development), TESDA skills training, NCIP for indigenous communities; align programs to BuildRight offtake needs
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Agency Liaison
Accountable (A): Sustainability/ESG Manager
Duration: Per partnership</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3119_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3119_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3119_Task5" name="Sustainability Lead structures co-funding/grant: BuildRight provides offtake…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sustainability Lead structures co-funding/grant: BuildRight provides offtake commitment + technical assist; government provides seed grant/ equipment/ training; coop commits to livelihood outcomes; Legal reviews MOA
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per partnership</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3119_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3119_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3119_Task6" name="Sustainability Lead reports livelihood outcomes to government partner and into…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Sustainability Lead reports livelihood outcomes to government partner and into BuildRight impact scorecard (links to W3129); sustains partnership across program cycles
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): Sustainability/ESG Manager
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3119_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3119_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3119_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3119_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3119_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-511 (ensure controlled execution — Cooperative &amp; Social Enterprise Sourcing Strategy &amp; Onboarding (PA-94.1).) | - operational: agency-level (not personality-level) MOA and multi-partner diversification
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
